frame 10
  default: One of the five, Gaussian forward noise, is a free choice. The other four are bets about the data and the network.

frame 11
  default: Convnet: each output looks at a small neighbourhood with the same filter everywhere, a built-in bet that nearby pixels matter most.
  switch 1 flipped: Transformer: every patch compares itself with every other patch from the first layer, with fewer built-in bets about distance.

frame 12
  default: Three scenes, one toy each: ten heights, a 2 × 2 image, four dogs. The same moves carry across: a density, a fixed map from noise, and Bayes to go back.

